COMPLETE TASK LIST — DATASET 3

Datasets : Kaggle (Walmart sales data)
________________________________________
1. Data Ingestion & Temporal Sanity Checks
•	Load daily sales data
•	Load calendar data (holidays, events)
•	Load promotions/pricing data
•	Inspect shapes and schemas
•	Parse dates explicitly
•	Enforce timezone consistency
•	Sort strictly by time
•	Verify monotonic time index
•	Detect duplicate (date, store, item) keys
•	Validate temporal granularity (daily vs weekly)
•	Detect implicit aggregation (daily totals vs transactions)
•	Validate units:
o	Quantity
o	Revenue
o	Price
•	Identify temporal keys vs entity keys
🚨 Titanic trap avoided: Row order now matters.
________________________________________
2. Temporal Data Understanding & Semantics
•	Define prediction target:
o	next-day sales
o	next-week demand
•	Identify forecast horizon
•	Identify availability lag (labels known when?)
•	Identify features known at prediction time
•	Identify forbidden future features
•	Validate business logic:
o	promotions start/end dates
o	stockout indicators
•	Separate event-time vs observation-time semantics
________________________________________
3. Temporal Data Quality Checks
•	Missing date detection
•	Missing entity-time combinations
•	Duplicate temporal records
•	Temporal out-of-order events
•	Negative sales detection
•	Stockout vs zero-sales disambiguation
•	Calendar continuity checks
•	Holiday alignment validation
•	Sudden regime shifts detection
•	Latency distribution analysis
________________________________________
4. Combining Multiple Datasets (Time-Aware Integration)
Pre-Join Temporal Analysis
•	Validate join keys including time
•	Check alignment resolution (day/hour)
•	Identify many-to-many temporal join risks
•	Detect overlapping validity windows
•	Analyze key coverage across time
Relational Joins
•	Left joins for enrichment
•	Join indicator diagnostics
•	Orphan record detection
•	Row explosion detection
Time-Aware Joins (Critical)
•	Exact timestamp joins (failure case)
•	As-of joins (canonical)
•	Forward-only joins (causal)
•	Backward joins (diagnostic)
•	Tolerance-window joins
•	Lag-aligned joins
•	Validity-interval joins (promo windows)
🚨 Titanic trap avoided: “Merge works” ≠ “Join is valid”.
